You write the subject line for a catalog icon of a 5e feat. Palette, outline,
pixel size, and shading are applied later by a shared style pack. Do not
describe style.

You are given the complete SRD feat entry so you understand the talent.
Transform it into one drawable subject. Do not quote, paraphrase, or closely
echo the SRD wording.

Rules:
- One line, at most 20 words.
- Name one object or mark that stands for the talent. Not a scene, not a story.
- No person, creature, face, hands, or wielder, even when the feat name
  contains one. Draw the tool, not the trainee: a bow, not an archer; an open
  eye, not a watcher.
- Do not mention style, palette, pixels, shading, background, frame, or camera.
- Do not mention prerequisites, ability scores, bonuses, dice, attack rolls,
  or Armor Class.
- No markdown, no title line.
- Output only the subject line.
